{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChRBsSUPoDkSBHKu3rYsQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Q5J9x7R2sdpA9aXnj5JNoZ","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"git log --oneline origin/main 2>/dev/null | grep -E \"#(346|302|303)\\b\" | head; git log --oneline -5; ls .ard/346 .ard/302 2>/dev/null; head -8 .ard/346/*.md .ard/302/*.md 2>/dev/null | head -60; grep -rn \"SetRepoVariable\\|ARD_BOT_LOGIN\\|print-workflow\" --include=*.go . | head; ls .github/workflows 2>/dev/null"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2309,"cache_read_input_tokens":9084,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2309},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7ab0f61a-33b6-435b-b709-eed90630048d","uuid":"25ef275c-fb7a-4d63-9021-719655b6fec1","timestamp":"2026-11-26T08:01:11.960Z","request_id":"req_011ChRBsSLD69AQnv1HCH9hQ"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Q5J9x7R2sdpA9aXnj5JNoZ","type":"tool_result","content":"deeeab9 prompts: sync the live .ard/ prompts with the starters, keeping the review-round text (#442)\nb9b7865 feat: ard serve: check GitHub connectivity at startup, accept a… (#302) (#445)\n7bcfa54 feat: Conflict rounds, part B: worker merge resolution and the c… (#323) (#443)\ncc5b043 chore: Log secret scan: AWS's documented example key is a false… (#355) (#444)\ncb3f0ea ard(worker:engineer): #302 `ard serve` now checks GitHub connectivity and permissions before any l… [skip ci]\n.ard/302:\ncosts\nlogs\nplan.md\nreview-eng-review.md\ntriage-engineer.md\ntriage-lead.md\nworker-engineer.md\n\n.ard/346:\ncosts\nlogs\nplan.md\nreview-eng-review.md\ntriage-engineer.md\ntriage-lead.md\nworker-engineer.md\n==> .ard/346/plan.md <==\n# Plan for #346\n\n## Implementation\n\nDecision on the open point from triage: this issue does **not** build the shared permission check. #302 owns `github.Connect` (not on main yet), so a second one here would conflict. Setup takes the check through a seam (`Deps.Permissions`) and this change wires a minimal default (repo readable with the configured auth). When #302 lands, one line in `cmd/ard/main.go` swaps in an adapter over `github.Connect`. The worker must not create `internal/github/connect.go`.\n\n### Steps\n\n\n==> .ard/346/review-eng-review.md <==\n---\nrole: eng-review\nstatus: done\nattempt: 1\nverdict: approve\n---\nThe `ard setup` change matches the plan and the issue, and its tests cover the exit-2, manual-steps, dry-run, idempotence and never-delete paths. Approved.\n\n\n==> .ard/346/triage-engineer.md <==\n---\nrole: engineer\nstatus: done\nattempt: 1\n---\nAdds a new `internal/setupcmd` package and an `ard setup` command that runs its checks, then applies the `ard:*` label sync only when the permission check is green. It supports `--check` (exit 2 on drift) and `--dry-run`, and `ard labels sync` stays as an alias. Size M, risk low to medium.\n\n## Open issues\n\n==> .ard/346/triage-lead.md <==\n---\nrole: lead\nstatus: done\nattempt: 1\nnext: [triage:engineer]\nworker: engineer\n---\nThis adds the first version of the `ard setup` command: a new setup package, CLI wiring, a check-then-apply flow with `--check` and `--dry-run`, the shared permission check, and `ard:*` label sync that reuses the existing labelsync code. Its stated dependency, the #343 design docs, has already landed on main, so the work can start now. Only the engineer triage role exists, so it plans the whole change.\n\n==> .ard/346/worker-engineer.md <==\n---\nrole: engineer\nstatus: done\nattempt: 1\n---\nAdds `ard setup`: it runs every check (origin/main comparison warning, permissions, `ard:*` labels), then applies label fixes. `--check` reports only and exits 2 on drift. `ard labels sync` stays as an alias.\n\n## Changes\n\n==> .ard/302/plan.md <==\n# Plan for #302\n\n## Implementation\n\nDecision on self-review (the one open choice): no reviewer change is needed. `internal/reviewer` already posts every review with event COMMENT (`github.ReviewInput` is \"always posted with event COMMENT\"), and ard's verdicts are gated on its own `.ard/<issue#>/` records, not on GitHub approvals. The only approval gate is the merger's protected-path check, `approved()` in `internal/merger/gates.go`, which already ignores reviews by `self` (ard's login). With a PAT, `self` is the token's user, so that user's own approval is ignored (GitHub also forbids approving your own PR). Behaviour: **a PAT setup needs protected-path approvals from a different write-access user**; the docs say so and a test pins it. A maintainer may want to confirm this.\n\n### Steps\n\n\n(eval):1: no matches found: --include=*.go\nbot-commits.yml\nci.yml\ndocs.yml\nrelease.yml\nversion.yml","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7ab0f61a-33b6-435b-b709-eed90630048d","uuid":"949ecb69-4ecd-4cf8-88c4-5db7a457596e","